.Dd 6 November 2026
.Dt SPIDER_IMAGE_COMPARE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm spider_image_compare
.Nd compare two images
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm spider_image_compare
.Op Fl frVv
.Op Fl b Ar background
.Op Fl l Ar window_level
.Op Fl o Ar output_directory
.Op Fl w Ar window_width
.Ar image1 image2
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
writes PNG images in which colour conveys the relative pixel values of
corresponding pixels in
.Ar image1
and
.Ar image2 ,
which are 3D scalar images with matching size, spacing, origin, and
direction.
Relative pixel values are determined separately for each input image.
A pixel that has a small relative pixel value in both images has
little colour; one that has a large relative value in
.Ar image1
and a small relative value in
.Ar image2
approaches yellow; one that has a small relative value in
.Ar image1
and a large relative value in
.Ar image2
approaches blue; and one that has a large relative value in both
images approaches magenta.
.Pp
A PNG image is written for each slice along the third image dimension.
PNG images are written in the current directory, unless the
.Fl o
option is specified.
Output files are named "slice_001.png", "slice_002.png", etc.
.Pp
.Ar image1
and
.Ar image2
may be in NIfTI format, compressed or not.
MetaImage and NRRD formats are also supported if the corresponding
ImageIO module is included in the ITK library against which
.Nm
was built.
The image files must each have a file name suffix corresponding to
their respective file formats.
For MetaImage and NRRD detached header formats, the name of the header
file must be specified.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b Ar background
Use the 3D scalar image
.Ar background
as a greyscale background in the PNG images.
It is expected to be co-registered with
.Ar image1
but may have different size, spacing, origin, and direction.
The supported file formats and file name suffix requirements are the
same as for
.Ar image1
and
.Ar image2 .
.Pp
.It Fl f
Overwrite output files.
.Pp
.It Fl l Ar window_level
Set the window level for the background image specified by
.Fl b .
No window is applied unless both
.Fl l
and
.Fl w
are specified.
.Pp
.It Fl o Ar output_directory
Write the PNG images to
.Ar output_directory .
.Ar output_directory
must already exist.
.Pp
.It Fl r
Reverse the row order in the PNG images.
.Pp
.It Fl V
Display the version number and exit.
.Pp
.It Fl v
Verbose mode.
Causes
.Nm
to print debugging messages about its progress.
.Pp
.It Fl w Ar window_width
Set the window width for the background image specified by
.Fl b .
No window is applied unless both
.Fl l
and
.Fl w
are specified.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr spider 1
